# Alembic Migration Directory

This directory contains database migration scripts for the All-in-One SIS project.

## Directory Structure

```
alembic/
├── env.py           # Migration environment configuration
├── script.py.mako  # Template for new migration files
├── README          # This file
└── versions/       # Individual migration scripts
```

## Migration Commands

### Create a new migration
```bash
cd apps/api
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "description"
```

### Apply all migrations
```bash
cd apps/api
alembic upgrade head
```

### Rollback last migration
```bash
cd apps/api
alembic downgrade -1
```

### Rollback to specific revision
```bash
cd apps/api
alembic downgrade <revision_id>
```

### Show current migration
```bash
cd apps/api
alembic current
```

### Show migration history
```bash
cd apps/api
alembic history
```

### Show SQL for pending migrations (without running)
```bash
cd apps/api
alembic upgrade --sql
```

## Using Make Commands

From project root:
```bash
make migrate                  # Apply all migrations
make create-migration msg=    # Create new migration
make rollback                # Rollback last migration
```

## Notes

- All models are imported in `env.py` to ensure autogenerate detects all changes
- The migration environment uses async SQLAlchemy engine
- Target metadata comes from `app.models.base.Base`
